      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first term and the common ratio of the geometric series.\n2. Use the formula for the sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series.\n3. Determine the number of terms in the series.\n4. Substitute the known values into the sum formula and calculate the sum.\n\nThe given series is \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\). This is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common ratio \\(r = 2\\).\n\nFirst, we need to determine the number of terms \\(n\\) in the series. The \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series can be expressed as:\n\\[a \\cdot r^{n-1}\\]\nWe know the last term \\(a_n = 1024\\). So, we can set up the equation:\n\\[1 \\cdot 2^{n-1} = 1024\\]\n\\[2^{n-1} = 1024\\]\nSince \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\), we have:\n\\[2^{n-1} = 2^{10}\\]\nThis implies:\n\\[n-1 = 10\\]\n\\[n = 11\\]\nSo, there are 11 terms in the series.\n\nNow, we use the sum formula for the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series:\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\\]\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[S_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1\\]\nWe know that \\(2^{11} = 2048\\), so:\n\\[S_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\\]\nTherefore, the sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is:\n\\[\\boxed{2047}\\]",
