      "text": "This math problem involves an arithmetic sequence where the first term is 1 and the common difference is also 1. To find the sum of an arithmetic series, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(2a + (n-1)d) \\]\n\nwhere \\( S_n \\) is the sum of the first \\( n \\) terms, \\( a \\) is the first term, \\( d \\) is the common difference, and \\( n \\) is the number of terms.\n\nIn this case, \\( a = 1 \\), \\( d = 1 \\), and the last term \\( l = 1024 \\). We need to find the number of terms \\( n \\) first.\n\nThe last term \\( l \\) of an arithmetic sequence can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ l = a + (n-1)d \\]\n\nPlugging in the values, we get:\n\n\\[ 1024 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 1 \\]\n\\[ 1024 = 1 + n - 1 \\]\n\\[ 1024 = n \\]\n\nSo, there are 1024 terms in the sequence.\n\nNow we can use the sum formula:\n\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(2a + (n-1)d) \\]\n\nSubstituting \\( n = 1024 \\), \\( a = 1 \\), and \\( d = 1 \\):\n\n\\[ S_{1024} = \\frac{1024}{2}(2 \\cdot 1 + (1024-1) \\cdot 1) \\]\n\\[ S_{1024} = 512(2 + 1023) \\]\n\\[ S_{1024} = 512 \\cdot 1025 \\]\n\\[ S_{1024} = 520300 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the arithmetic sequence \\( 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024 \\) is \\(\\boxed{520300}\\).",
