      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first identify the common ratio and the number of terms in the series.\n\nThe first term \\(a\\) of the series is 1, and the common ratio \\(r\\) is 2. The \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series can be expressed as:\n\\[a_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1}\\]\n\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) such that the \\(n\\)-th term is 1024. Setting \\(a_n = 1024\\), we get:\n\\[1024 = 1 \\cdot 2^{n-1} \\implies 2^{n-1} = 1024\\]\nSince \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\), we have:\n\\[2^{n-1} = 2^{10} \\implies n-1 = 10 \\implies n = 11\\]\n\nSo, there are 11 terms in the series. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[S_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{1} = 2^{11} - 1\\]\n\nCalculating \\(2^{11}\\):\n\\[2^{11} = 2048\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum is:\n\\[S_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\\]\n\nThe sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is \\(\\boxed{2047}\\).",
